    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by the elite matchup facing **Kyle Tucker** (81.09) and **Andy Pages** (72.03) against Grayson Rodriguez, whose 17.18 xERA presents a massive ceiling opportunity. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) remains our strongest middle-infielder play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Young and a significant +14% boost due to dynamic platoon splits. While **Josh Lowe** (72.20) sits in the bottom third of the order, he remains a high-floor start because of his elite speed profile and the advantageous matchup against the porous Sasaki. Despite a headwind dampening his power output, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.48) remains a locked-in start, as his high-contact floor effectively insulates him against the risk of the stadium environment.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (57.80), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Sam Antonacci** (57.27) and **Dominic Smith** (56.54). While **Coby Mayo** offers significant power, **Sam Antonacci** was prioritized due to his elite 0.400 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot against Rea, providing more stability for our AVG and R categories. We are also closely monitoring the lineup risks for **Gunnar Henderson** (62.99); although he is a defensive anchor, his score is currently suppressed by a -15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against Lovelady. We are keeping **Jackson Merrill** (51.66) and **Miguel Vargas** (51.68) in reserve today to manage game caps, as their scores against tough arms like Kirby do not justify the risk to our remaining roster efficiency for the rest of the month.",
